From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: finalpantasy <finalpantasy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 08:33:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 12/34] Inline CRT math imports in the lifter; import and map
 stats; POSIX ExeDir

The manifest `crt` directive now also takes memcmp and the float math the
game calls through import stubs (sqrtf, sqrt, floorf, ceilf, fmodf, sinf,
cosf, tanf, asinf, acosf, expf, logf, atan2f, powf), plus _isnan and
_finite, which are called straight through their import slots. Exact
functions inline as std::; the rest call recomp::crt (x86/crt_math.h),
the same correctly rounded and errno path as the HLE handlers.

FFXII_IMPORT_STATS (hle.cpp) logs the 40 most-called imports every 30 s;
RECOMP_D3D_MAP_STATS (d3d11.cpp) counts Map types per resource kind.
ExeDir is now defined on POSIX hosts too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
